WEBVTT

NOTE Module 01 transcript — auto-aligned to narration.wav (128.4s). en.

1
00:00:00.192 --> 00:00:04.413
Welcome to Module One — an introduction to deep learning and TensorFlow.

2
00:00:05.623 --> 00:00:19.831
In the next minute: what deep learning actually is, why it took over machine learning this decade, and the three ideas it all rests on — representations, the chain rule, and gradient descent.

3
00:00:21.763 --> 00:00:26.714
The big shift that started it all: moving from hand-crafted features to learned ones.

4
00:00:27.562 --> 00:00:30.752
A deep network is just a stack of differentiable functions.

5
00:00:31.106 --> 00:00:35.661
Its power comes from composition — not one clever layer.

6
00:00:36.045 --> 00:00:42.850
Training means minimizing a single loss with gradient descent, and gradients flow backward through the chain rule.

7
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.348
So why did all of this happen now?

8
00:00:47.678 --> 00:01:01.367
Three things converged: AlexNet on ImageNet in twenty-twelve halved error rates, GPUs unlocked massive training, and tricks like ReLU and batch norm made depth stable — all wrapped in open-source frameworks.

9
00:01:02.341 --> 00:01:06.658
The stack you'll use for that is TensorFlow and Keras.

10
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.713
Tensors are arrays that live on CPU or GPU.

11
00:01:11.088 --> 00:01:14.155
T-F-dot-function compiles your Python into a graph.

12
00:01:14.519 --> 00:01:17.932
Keras is the high-level API most courses teach.

13
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.587
And GradientTape handles differentiation when you write your own custom loops.

14
00:01:22.942 --> 00:01:24.717
Here's gradient descent in thirty seconds.

15
00:01:25.072 --> 00:01:30.051
Pick a loss that measures how wrong you are.

16
00:01:30.378 --> 00:01:33.516
Compute its gradient with respect to the parameters.

17
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.525
Step against that gradient.

18
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:44.250
Repeat on mini-batches until the loss plateaus — and everything else in this course is variance reduction on that one loop.

19
00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.237
Here's the road ahead.

20
00:01:48.245 --> 00:01:54.295
Ten modules — fundamentals, CNNs, advanced training, segmentation, detection, GANs, NLP, time series, and production.

21
00:01:55.022 --> 00:01:58.007
Each has theory, hands-on labs, and a quiz.

22
00:01:59.207 --> 00:02:02.572
And your progress stays on your device.

23
00:02:02.943 --> 00:02:07.633
Let's get started — open the first lab.
